; dsv4-decode-form-band.fk — what the Form-held DS4 decode loop can actually stand on today.
;
; PROOF LEVEL: METAL-LINKED fkwu ONLY. This band drives a real GPU through the handle door and reads a
; real 9.1 GB GGUF, so it has exactly one home arm:
;     cc -O2 -o fkwu-metal runtime/fkwu-uni.c form/native/metal/fk-metal-carrier.m \
;        -framework Metal -framework Foundation -fobjc-arc
;     ./fkwu-metal --src form/form-stdlib/tests/dsv4-decode-form-band.fk
; On any other arm metal_status answers metal_linked=false and bit 1 does not light, which takes the
; whole verdict with it — that is the intended SKIP, and it is spoken rather than silent.
;
; WHAT THIS BAND REFUSES TO CLAIM. The standing task is a 43-layer decode whose token stream matches
; metal_dsv4_stack.sh bit for bit. That is NOT proven here and there is no bit for it. Seven bits, and
; every one of them is something this session ran. An eighth bit for "argmax agrees with the oracle"
; would be a fold over `nothing` — the failure this body calls numb-green — because there is no stack
; yet to take an argmax of. The gap is named in dsv4-decode-form.fk's UNFINISHED block, not papered.
;
; WHY THE GATE IS metal_status AND NOT A NUMBER. Every other primitive on this door answers an INTEGER
; handle, and an unbound name under axiom-5 recovers to nothing and answers 0. A 0 from a door that was
; never linked, a 0 from a door that refused, and a 0 from a typo are the same shape. metal_status is
; the one primitive whose answer cannot be counterfeited by a numb call, so bit 1 is checked first and
; every later bit is worthless without it.
;
; WHY BIT 2 IS PINNED TO LITERALS AND NOT TO AGREEMENT WITH ITSELF. The cell reads the geometry by
; walking the file's header. Comparing that walk to itself proves nothing: a wrong offset would make
; the GPU and the CPU cross-check read the SAME wrong bytes and agree perfectly. So the five numbers
; below are pinned to what an INDEPENDENT ARM printed — form-kernel-go/bin-go running
; gm-emit-manifest over the same file, which answered:
;     T token_embd.weight 1 2 4096 129280 1 71707886176 529530880 1 1059061760
; Same recipe, different kernel. A literal cannot drift with the code that produced it.
;
; Verdict 8388607 when the five rungs are honest:
;   1   the door SPEAKS — metal_status carries metal_linked=true (the voice canary, checked first)
;   2   the geometry is READ FROM THE HEADER and matches the Go arm's manifest literally:
;       n_embd 4096, vocab 129280, ggml type 1 (F16), absolute offset 71707886176, bytes 1059061760
;   4   the weights are the FILE'S OWN PAGES — metal_status reports a nocopy mmap buffer, so the
;       9.1 GB never crossed the host membrane as a copy; reading the model file is the one permitted
;       crossing and this proves it stayed that
;   8   the door ENQUEUED WITHOUT WAITING — the batch was still open when the read drained it
;   16  EVERY lane of the embedding row is bit-exact against this body's own f16->f32 widening,
;       bad=0 AND odd=0 (a fold over all n_embd, no epsilon, no sampling, nothing excused)
;   32  the fp-contract pragma this cell emits ACTUALLY suppresses contraction through this door —
;       checked, not asserted, because the door compiles with options:nil and contracts by default
;  128  RMSNORM ON SYNTHETIC TRUTH, EXACT. x=2.0, g=1.0, eps=0 -> inv must be 0x3F000000 and every
;       lane exactly 0x3F800000. Hand-computed, no tolerance, no tool. The strongest bit in rung 2.
;  256  blk.0.attn_norm.weight sits at the address the Go arm printed (72877251424) and is n_embd wide
;  512  the REDUCE agrees with a Form fp64 fold over the same bytes, via implied mean-square
;       (1/inv^2 - eps), which needs no sqrt on the reference side. Tolerance 1e-6; measured 1.03e-7.
;       GATED on the row address pin — see below.
; 1024  the APPLY agrees with the fp64 reference against the VECTOR'S SCALE (overfine, row 934),
;       not each element's own magnitude. Tolerance 1e-6; measured 6.25e-8. GATED on the row pin AND
;       on bit 256, because the reference reads the norm weights through the same address the GPU got.
;       WITHOUT THOSE GATES BOTH BITS WERE COMOVED AND PROVED NOTHING: mutation N5 (embed the wrong
;       row) answered 2047, and N1 (output_norm.weight in place of blk.0.attn_norm.weight) answered
;       1791 where 767 was predicted. The relative error is only evidence once the addresses are pinned.
; 2048  THE MXFP8 FUSED MATVEC ON SYNTHETIC TRUTH, EXACT. Payload byte 56 (E4M3 1.0) and scale byte
;       127 (E8M0 2^0 = 1.0) with x = 1.0 gives y[r] = cols = 4096.0 = 0x45800000 on every row, and
;       every partial sum is an integer below 2^24 so it is exact under ANY association. That is the
;       bit's strength and its stated limit: it proves the decode, the scale-plane origin at nel, and
;       that every column was visited exactly once -- and it is BLIND to association, which is what
;       ds4-order-match.fk exists for. Bit 8192 is not its evidence and it is not bit 8192's.
; 4096  blk.0.attn_q_a.weight is where the Go arm said (72838323040), type 41, 1024x4096. The file's
;       own byte count 4325376 equals nel + nel/32, so the plane-split layout is confirmed by
;       arithmetic before any kernel reads it.
; 8192  the real projection (embed -> rmsnorm -> MXFP8 matvec, four dispatches, ONE sync) agrees with
;       the body's own mxp8-at reader folded in fp64 over eight rows, judged against the ROW VECTOR'S
;       SCALE. Measured 68 ppb. Per ELEMENT the same disagreement reads 1018 ppb purely because
;       y[0] = 0.017 is a near-cancellation of terms of scale 0.1 -- overfine, row 934, is exactly
;       this case. GATED on bit 4096 and on the row pin. EIGHT rows of 1024, because each is a
;       4096-term fp64 fold in Form; a fault confined to high row indices would not be seen.
; 16384 THE FOLD-ORDER WITNESS, the bit the uniform synthetics cannot be. Weights 1.0, x[0] = 2^24,
;       x[1..31] = 1.0, rest 0. fp64 truth is 2^24+31; the kernel's stated ascending in-group fold
;       lands each +1 on a tie-to-even that rounds BACK to 2^24, so the f32 answer is EXACTLY
;       0x4B800000 — and a reversed or pairwise fold answers 2^24+32, sixteen bits away. Verified by
;       f32-step simulation before the kernel ran. From the attention split onward order is the whole
;       question (ds4-order-match.fk), and this is the reusable instrument for it.
; 32768 rung-4 geometry, all four tensors at the Go arm's addresses: q_a_norm 72766950240,
;       kv_a_norm 72766948192, q_b 72842648416 [32768 x 1024], kv 72766954336.
; 65536 both rank-space rmsnorms agree with the fp64 reference (tn-sqrt, the body's Newton spine):
;       measured 120 ppb (q, n=1024) and 77 ppb (k, n=512) against the vector's scale.
; 131072 the q_b projection (type 41, 8 of 32768 rows) agrees: measured 178 ppb.
; 262144 headrms over ALL 64 heads agrees: measured 429 ppb — above the other steps because the
;       kernel's mla_sqrt is f32 Newton against the reference's fp64 Newton, still 2000x under the
;       bar. The chain is covered by induction: each step's reference reads the GPU's INPUT for that
;       step (the previous step's separately-checked output buffer) and weights at pinned addresses.
; 524288 blk.0.attn_sinks.weight at the Go arm's 72766947936, AND freqs[0] == 0x3F800000 exactly —
;       pow(base, 0) = 1 is an identity of the function, not a tolerance. The freqs are computed ON
;       THE DEVICE by a cell-emitted kernel and read back; the fp64 rope reference widens those same
;       bits, so a wrong pow cannot agree its way past this bit.
; 1048576 RoPE at pos 7: the NOPE dims (448 per head, k row + q head 0) are BIT-EQUAL through the
;       kernel — a copy is checked as a copy — and the rotated tails agree with fcos/fsin in fp64:
;       measured 236 ppb against the tail's scale. Layer 0 is a ratio-0 raw-regime layer; the
;       compressed-base reduction (layer 2+) is NOT claimed by this bit.
; 2097152 the sink-softmax attention (one KV row, 64 heads) agrees with mla-attn.fk's softmax shape
;       folded in fp64 (tn-exp, tn-sqrt): measured 886 ppb — the widest step yet because mla_exp is
;       an f32 Taylor against fp64, still under the bar. scale = 1/sqrt(512) rides as f32 bits
;       1026884851; the reference derives its own from tn-sqrt, so the literal is cross-checked.
;   64  the token's row lands at the absolute address an INDEPENDENT computation says it must:
;       71707886176 + 671*4096*2 = 77933529920. THIS BIT WAS ADDED BECAUSE THE BAND FAILED A
;       MUTATION WITHOUT IT (M2, embed the wrong row: predicted 47, band answered 63). bit16 now
;       depends on it, so a perfect fold over the wrong row can no longer read green.
;
; preludes: native/metal/dsv4-decode-form.fk

(do
    (defn dfb-model () "/Users/ursmuff/models/ds4-engine/gguf/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-IQ2XXS-w2Q2K-AProjQ8-SExpQ8-OutQ8-chat-v2-imatrix.gguf")
    (defn dfb-token () 671)

    ; bit 1 — the voice canary. str_find answers -1 when absent, so a numb door cannot light this.
    (defn dfb-linked? (st) (if (ge (str_find st "metal_linked=true" 0) 0) 1 0))
    (defn dfb-nocopy? (st) (if (ge (str_find st "mmap_nocopy_buffers=0" 0) 0) 0 1))
    ; the read drains the batch, so after it the door must report the dispatches DONE and the batch
    ; empty. pending>0 here would mean the read did not sync; total_dispatch=0 would mean nothing ran.
    (defn dfb-enqueued? (st)
        (if (ge (str_find st "pending=0" 0) 0)
            (if (ge (str_find st "total_dispatch=0" 0) 0) 0 1)
            0))

    (defn dfb-geom? (f)
        (if (eq (nth f 3) 4096)
            (if (eq (nth f 4) 129280)
                (if (eq (nth f 5) 1)
                    (if (eq (nth f 6) 77928033088)
                        (if (eq (nth f 7) 1059061760) 1 0) 0) 0) 0) 0))

    ; bit 64 — THE ROW ITSELF, and this bit exists because the band FAILED a mutation without it.
    ; Mutation M2 made the cell embed token+1 instead of token. Predicted 47; the band answered 63.
    ; It caught nothing, because the reference bytes were read at the SAME computed row offset the
    ; GPU used, so a wrong row moved BOTH sides together and they agreed perfectly about the wrong
    ; place. That is precisely the self-referential trap this band's own header warns about for the
    ; geometry — written down, and then not applied one field over. The cure is the same cure: pin the
    ; row's absolute address to a literal, computed independently of the code under test as
    ;     71707886176 + 671 * 4096 * 2 = 77933529920
    ; A literal cannot drift with the arithmetic that produced it.
    (defn dfb-rowaddr? (f) (if (eq (nth f 9) 77933529920) 1 0))

    ; bit 16 — the fold. ok must equal n_embd exactly AND bad and odd must both be zero AND the row
    ; must be the right row. Demanding all four is the point: ok=n_embd with odd>0 would mean lanes
    ; were skipped rather than passed, and a perfect fold over the WRONG row is worth nothing at all.
    (defn dfb-exact? (f)
        (if (eq (dfb-rowaddr? f) 1)
            (if (eq (nth f 0) (nth f 3))
                (if (eq (nth f 1) 0) (if (eq (nth f 2) 0) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))

    ; ── RUNG 2 anchors. rel1/rel2 are fp32-vs-fp64 MAGNITUDE checks and the tolerance is stated
    ; rather than discovered: measured 103 ppb (reduce) and 63 ppb (apply), which is f32 rounding
    ; scale (f32 eps ~119 ppb) over a 4096-term fold. The bar is 1e-6 — ~10x the observed noise and
    ; ~4 orders below any structural error, which lands at 1e-2 or worse. These are NOT bit-exactness
    ; and this band does not call them that; bit 128 is the exact one.
    (defn dfb-tol () 0.000001)
    (defn dfb-rmsgeom? (f2 n)
        (if (eq (nth f2 2) 79100740672) (if (eq (nth f2 4) n) 1 0) 0))

    (let facts (dfd-embed (dfb-model) (dfb-token)))
    (let st (nth facts 8))
    (let b1  (dfb-linked? st))
    (let b2  (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-geom? facts) 0))
    (let b4  (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-nocopy? st) 0))
    (let b8  (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-enqueued? st) 0))
    (let b16 (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-exact? facts) 0))
    (let b32 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-contract-ok?) 0))
    (let b64 (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-rowaddr? facts) 0))
    (let b128 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-rmsnorm-synth (nth facts 3)) 0))
    (let rung2 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-rmsnorm-rung (dfb-model) (dfb-token)) 0))
    (let b256 (if (eq b1 1) (dfb-rmsgeom? rung2 (nth facts 3)) 0))
    ; bits 512/1024 are GATED ON THE PINNED ADDRESSES, not only on the relative error. A relative
    ; error computed against a reference that read the same wrong bytes is not evidence of anything.
    (let rowpin (if (eq (nth rung2 5) 77933529920) 1 0))
    (let b512 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq rowpin 1) (if (lt (nth rung2 0) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0))
    (let b1024 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq rowpin 1) (if (eq b256 1) (if (lt (nth rung2 1) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))
    ; ── RUNG 3: the MXFP8 q_a projection
    (let b2048 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-mx8-synth 1024 4096) 0))
    (let rung3 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-mla-rung (dfb-model) (dfb-token)) 0))
    (let b4096 (if (eq b1 1)
                   (if (eq (nth rung3 1) 79060632640)
                       (if (eq (nth rung3 2) 1024) (if (eq (nth rung3 3) 4096) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))
    (let rowpin3 (if (eq (nth rung3 4) 77933529920) 1 0))
    (let b8192 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq b4096 1) (if (eq rowpin3 1)
                   (if (lt (nth rung3 0) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))
    ; ── RUNG 4: q_a_norm/kv_a_norm, q_b, headrms — and the fold-ORDER witness
    (let b16384 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-mx8-ordersynth) 0))
    (let rung4 (if (eq b1 1) (dfd-mla2-rung (dfb-model) (dfb-token)) 0))
    (let b32768 (if (eq b1 1)
        (if (eq (nth rung4 4) 78987097152)
            (if (eq (nth rung4 5) 78987095104)
                (if (eq (nth rung4 6) 79065089088)
                    (if (eq (nth rung4 7) 78987101248)
                        (if (eq (nth rung4 9) 32768)
                            (if (eq (nth rung4 10) 1024) 1 0) 0) 0) 0) 0) 0) 0))
    (let rowpin4 (if (eq (nth rung4 8) 77933529920) 1 0))
    (let gate4 (if (eq b32768 1) rowpin4 0))
    (let b65536 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1)
        (if (lt (nth rung4 0) (dfb-tol)) (if (lt (nth rung4 1) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))
    (let b131072 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1) (if (lt (nth rung4 2) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0))
    (let b262144 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1) (if (lt (nth rung4 3) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0))
    ; ── RUNG 5: RoPE + sink-softmax attention (same chain, four more dispatches)
    ; freqs[1] is pinned against fpow(10000, -1/32) computed IN FORM fp64 — 10000.0 is the file's own
    ; deepseek4.rope.freq_base as the Go arm printed it. Without this, the cell's base literal and the
    ; rope reference are COMOVED: the reference widens the freqs the GPU computed, so a wrong base
    ; agrees with itself perfectly. freqs[0] cannot see it (pow(b,0)=1 for every b); freqs[1] can.
    (let f1ref (fpow 10000.0 (div -1.0 32.0)))
    (let f1got (fd-value (nth rung4 16) 8 23))
    (let f1ok (if (lt (div (abs (sub f1got f1ref)) f1ref) (dfb-tol)) 1 0))
    (let b524288 (if (eq b1 1)
        (if (eq (nth rung4 14) 78987094848)
            (if (eq (nth rung4 15) 1065353216) f1ok 0) 0) 0))
    (let b1048576 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1) (if (eq b524288 1)
        (if (eq (nth rung4 13) 896) (if (lt (nth rung4 11) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0) 0))
    (let b2097152 (if (eq b1 1) (if (eq gate4 1) (if (eq b524288 1)
        (if (lt (nth rung4 12) (dfb-tol)) 1 0) 0) 0) 0))

    (print (str_concat "bit1  door speaks          = " (int_to_str b1)))
    (print (str_concat "bit2  geometry from header = " (int_to_str b2)))
    (print (str_concat "bit4  mmap nocopy          = " (int_to_str b4)))
    (print (str_concat "bit8  enqueue without wait = " (int_to_str b8)))
    (print (str_concat "bit16 embedding bit-exact  = " (int_to_str b16)))
    (print (str_concat "bit32 contraction off      = " (int_to_str b32)))
    (print (str_concat "bit64 token row address    = " (int_to_str b64)))
    (print (str_concat "bit128 rmsnorm synth exact = " (int_to_str b128)))
    (print (str_concat "bit256 attn_norm geometry  = " (int_to_str b256)))
    (print (str_concat "bit512 rmsnorm reduce ref  = " (int_to_str b512)))
    (print (str_concat "bit1024 rmsnorm apply ref  = " (int_to_str b1024)))
    (print (str_concat "bit2048 mxfp8 synth exact  = " (int_to_str b2048)))
    (print (str_concat "bit4096 q_a geometry       = " (int_to_str b4096)))
    (print (str_concat "bit8192 q_a projection ref = " (int_to_str b8192)))
    (print (str_concat "bit16384 fold-ORDER witness = " (int_to_str b16384)))
    (print (str_concat "bit32768 rung4 geometry     = " (int_to_str b32768)))
    (print (str_concat "bit65536 rank norms ref     = " (int_to_str b65536)))
    (print (str_concat "bit131072 q_b projection ref= " (int_to_str b131072)))
    (print (str_concat "bit262144 headrms ref       = " (int_to_str b262144)))
    (print (str_concat "bit524288 sinks+freqs0 pins = " (int_to_str b524288)))
    (print (str_concat "bit1048576 rope ref+NOPE    = " (int_to_str b1048576)))
    (print (str_concat "bit2097152 attend ref       = " (int_to_str b2097152)))

    (let verdict (add b1 (add (mul 2 b2) (add (mul 4 b4)
                    (add (mul 8 b8) (add (mul 16 b16) (add (mul 32 b32) (add (mul 64 b64)
                    (add (mul 128 b128) (add (mul 256 b256)
                    (add (mul 512 b512) (add (mul 1024 b1024)
                    (add (mul 2048 b2048) (add (mul 4096 b4096)
                    (add (mul 8192 b8192) (add (mul 16384 b16384)
                    (add (mul 32768 b32768) (add (mul 65536 b65536)
                    (add (mul 131072 b131072) (add (mul 262144 b262144)
                    (add (mul 524288 b524288) (add (mul 1048576 b1048576)
                         (mul 2097152 b2097152)))))))))))))))))))))))
    (print (str_concat "Verdict: " (int_to_str verdict)))
    verdict)
